course: dictionary
lesson: 8264
title: Rider
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A rider is a person who rides something, such as a horse, a bike, a motorbike or a scooter. To ride means to sit on it and travel along with it.
explain: «When passing a horse and rider you slow down, give lots of room and say hello so the horse knows you are a person.» Here the rider is the person sitting on top of the horse, and the horse is the animal underneath.
explain: Look at the words around rider to see what is being ridden. Bike rider, horse rider, a good rider and motorbike rider all name the thing the person sits on. If someone is only sitting in a bus or train, the word may mean something different, as you will see in the facts.
fact: A rider is a person who rides a horse, a bike, a motorbike or a scooter.
fact: Phrases like «bike rider», «horse rider» and «motorbike rider» show what the person is riding.
fact: Bike riders wear helmets and use lights, and horse riders wear hard hats.
fact: Mostly in America, a rider is also a passenger on a bus or train.
fact: «Professional bull riders need to stay on for eight seconds.»
exercise: «When passing a horse and rider you slow down.» What is the rider in this sentence? | The bag of food for the horse | The stable where the horse sleeps | *The person sitting on the horse | The wooden fence around the field
exercise: Which of these is a rider in everyday English? | A cup of hot cocoa on the table | *A girl on a scooter going to the park | A bridge over a river | A tree growing beside the road
exercise: Bike riders wear helmets and use lights. What do horse riders wear? | *A hard hat | A woolly scarf | A wet raincoat | A bright lamp
test: In «a motorbike rider», what is the rider sitting on? | A boat | A cloud | *A motorbike | A sofa
test: In America, a rider on a bus is best described as | A sign telling people the bus stop | *A passenger travelling on the bus | The driver who steers the bus | A machine that sells tickets
exam: «Nadia rides her scooter to school every day.» Who is the rider in this sentence? | The scooter | The road | *Nadia | The school
